WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.909
After rain and floods, standing water breeds mosquitoes,

2
00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:05.910
and mosquitoes spread malaria.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.940
Malaria can kill, especially young children and pregnant women.

4
00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:13.139
But it can be prevented, and it can be treated.

5
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.379
Here is how to protect your family.

6
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.512
Malaria is spread by the bite of an infected mosquito.

7
00:00:19.681 --> 00:00:22.922
Mosquitoes lay their eggs in still water: puddles,

8
00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:26.232
ditches and uncovered containers left after rain.

9
00:00:26.562 --> 00:00:31.232
The mosquitoes that carry malaria bite mostly from evening until morning.

10
00:00:31.441 --> 00:00:34.952
Fever usually starts ten to fifteen days after the bite.

11
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.310
First, sleep under an insecticide-treated mosquito net, every night.

12
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.270
Young children and pregnant women first, but everyone in the family.

13
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.950
Tuck the net in under the mattress or mat, all the way round,

14
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.580
so no mosquito can get in.

15
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.700
Mend any holes straight away.

16
00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:55.744
Second, take away the water mosquitoes breed in.

17
00:00:55.993 --> 00:00:59.944
Every week, empty and turn over old tins, tyres and pots.

18
00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:02.314
Keep water containers covered with a lid.

19
00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:05.664
Fill in or drain puddles and ditches near the house.

20
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.620
Third, stop the bites.

21
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.180
In the evening, wear long sleeves and cover your legs.

22
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.060
Use mosquito repellent on bare skin, as the label says.

23
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:20.300
If a health team comes to spray the inside of your house against mosquitoes,

24
00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:21.420
let them in.

25
00:01:22.306 --> 00:01:25.585
If anyone has a fever, go to a health facility the same day,

26
00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.506
and ask for a malaria test.

27
00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:30.096
A rapid test gives the answer in minutes.

28
00:01:30.106 --> 00:01:34.775
If it is malaria, take all of the medicine, exactly as the health worker says,

29
00:01:34.826 --> 00:01:36.576
even when you start to feel better.

30
00:01:36.706 --> 00:01:41.226
Go at once if the person has convulsions, is very sleepy, cannot drink,

31
00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.016
keeps vomiting, or has difficulty breathing.

32
00:01:44.026 --> 00:01:47.696
A young child with malaria can become very ill within a day.

33
00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:52.493
If you are pregnant, sleep under a net and go to antenatal care early,

34
00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:55.534
because malaria is dangerous for mother and baby.

35
00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:59.254
Nets every night, no standing water, test fever fast.

36
00:01:59.254 --> 00:02:00.803
Share this with your family.
